P1-4 is fixed in `/tmp/cc1-p1`, uncommitted.

**Base note:** `f440a2fb` is not present locally and fetching is barred (no ssh). The worktree therefore remains on `fa70516f` with the previous P1 fix already uncommitted in it. I built on that state rather than resetting and destroying it.

**Design choice:** the structural invariant, not an `assoc`-only patch. In [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:884), tracking metadata is now valid only for the exact vector object it was attached to. Every content-changing prelude primitive (`assoc`, `conj`, `vec`) routes its result through the single choke point `recover-rebuilt-packet` at [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:903), which drops `::origin-of` before lineage recovery. Extractive primitives (`first`, `get`) return the very tagged object, so they alone still trust its metadata. A rebuilt packet is re-provenanced only from its actual root/rows lineage; if no lineage entry accounts for it, it carries no provenance and is refused downstream as `:missing-provenance` rather than relabelled. In the repro, `(assoc a 0 (first b) 1 (first (rest b)))` now recovers `b`'s rows object from lineage and records the feed expansion's origin instead of `a`'s stale `[:source :program-in 0 0]`.

**Regression:** added the exact codex case as a new `testing` block in `p1-packet-provenance-test` at [clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1130), asserting `:ok`, a retained feed-expansion origin, never the stale source admission, and full call-site coverage validation.

